    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d634-a2">

                <pb facs="0804" n="710" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg710"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Nicaraguan Acting Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cordero
                            Reyes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American
                        Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Beaulac</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-02-10">February 10, 1930</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 17</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your Note No. 14 of February 8, 1930, with reference to a proposed agreement
                    between the Government of the United States of America and the Government of
                    Nicaragua under which the latter will grant to the United States Army Engineers
                    engaged in conducting a survey of the Nicaragua Canal Route free transportation
                    over the railroad and lake steamers belonging to the Pacific Railroad of
                    Nicaragua, in return for which those Engineers will carry out for the Government
                    of Nicaragua a survey of a rail route from Lake Nicaragua to the Atlantic Coast
                    via the San Juan River Valley.</p>
                <p>In reply, I beg to state to you that my Government accepts with the greatest
                    pleasure the agreement referred to as outlined in Paragraphs (1) and (2) of the
                    note to which I reply.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Cordero Reyes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
